   268	  translated closure body. `solution.py`, `solution.mpy`, `smoke.py`, and the
   269	  closure in `spec.k` agree. The material body mutation is rejected.
   270	- **A2 operational state preservation:** No source execution is bridged. The
   271	  loop claim executes the supplied rules and constrains or frames every active
   272	  cell. The only abstracted local value is dead after the loop.
   273	- **A3 binding/evaluation/control fidelity:** The module guard excludes a
   274	  shadowing `"min"` binding; the builtin scope is exact. Lookup, left-to-right
   275	  call argument evaluation, assignments, iteration, return, and frame popping
   276	  execute normally.
   277	- **A4 consistency/rule validity:** `allInts` is total. Summary functions cover
   278	  every admitted use and recurse on a strict tail. Both simplification lemmas
   279	  agree with supplied equations throughout their guards and on overlaps. No
   280	  opaque value or contradictory equation exists.
   281	- **A5 result constraint/non-vacuity:** `[5]` is a realizable witness. The false
   282	  result `6` is rejected with actual result `5`. Distinct-result witnesses in
   283	  the smoke suite include `[5] -> 5`, `[-1,-2,-3] -> -6`, and a mixed-sign
   284	  case.
   285	
   286	### Gate B — PASS
   287	
   288	- **B1 input domain:** The formal domain is exactly non-empty finite lists of
   289	  mathematical integers, matching the prompt's non-empty array of integers.
   290	- **B2 language model:** K `Int` and Python integers are unbounded; list order,
   291	  integer addition, integer comparison inside `minInt`, and non-mutating
   292	  iteration are material and modeled. Empty input is intentionally excluded.
   293	- **B3 summary/property:** The Kadane recurrence has the ending-subarray and
   294	  processed-prefix induction stated above. The K proof formally connects the
   295	  real program to the recurrence; the recurrence-to-prompt interpretation is
   296	  mathematically derived and independently tested against exhaustive
   297	  enumeration for the recorded finite domain.
   298	- **B4 implementation alignment:** Prompt examples and independent tests agree;
   299	  no implementation/specification discrepancy was found.
   300	
   301	### Gate C — PASS
   302	
   303	- All referenced artifacts exist in the workspace.
   304	- `prove.sh` records the exact build, concrete, positive-proof, and negative
   305	  probe commands and checks their expected exit behavior.
   306	- `smoke.py`/`smoke.mpy` exercise prompt examples and boundary/mixed-sign
   307	  cases under the supplied LLVM semantics.
   308	- `differential_test.py` uses a separately implemented nested-loop
   309	  brute-force oracle over every list of lengths `1..6` with values `-3..3`;
   310	  the recorded run checked 137,256 inputs with zero mismatches.
   311	- Finite evidence is reported only as evidence; the universal result comes
   312	  from `kprove`.
   313	
   314	## Trust boundary
   315	
   316	- The supplied, unmodified `reference-semantics/` definition, including K
   317	  builtin sort predicates/casts, `minInt`, integer hooks, and the Python subset
   318	  modeled there.
   319	- The K v7.1.293 compiler, LLVM/Haskell backends, solver, and reachability
   320	  prover.
   321	- The fixed, unmodified `py2mpy.py` transliterator and CPython AST parsing.
   322	- Manual syntactic alignment between the generated `solution.mpy` body and the
   323	  closure term in `spec.k`, supported by the concrete translated smoke module
   324	  and body mutation probe.
   325	- The mathematical induction relating the Kadane recurrence to the phrase
   326	  “minimum sum of any non-empty sub-array”; this intent bridge is independently
   327	  supported by the brute-force differential test but is not a separate
   328	  machine-checked combinatorial theorem.
   329	
   330	No task-specific external primitive or opaque result is trusted.
   331	
   332	## Empirically supported facts
   333	
   334	- All five K smoke assertions terminate without exception.
   335	- Both prompt examples produce the specified values.
   336	- Singleton, zero-only, all-negative, and mixed-sign examples agree.
   337	- The independent brute-force differential sample has zero mismatches over
   338	  137,256 arrays.
   339	- A material body mutation changes an observable result and is rejected.
   340	- A false postcondition on a satisfiable input is rejected.
   341	
   342	## Excluded behavior
   343	
   344	- Empty lists, non-integer elements, mutation/aliasing of the input, and Python
   345	  constructs outside the supplied semantics.
   346	- Total-correctness/liveness as a formal claim; K reachability here proves
   347	  partial correctness. Operationally, the supplied finite-list iterator
   348	  consumes one constructor per iteration.
   349	- Correctness of the supplied semantics, translator, K implementation, and
   350	  solver themselves.
   351	
   352	The runner marker is therefore `KPROVE_PASSED`: every required positive target
   353	proof command in `prove.sh` printed `#Top` and exited `0`. This marker is
   354	separate from the `VALIDATED` proof-quality headline above.

